        "payload": "tree 2b7dc02100e6c01ae61e9cc4ca44786296f33595\nparent 995da8678a02aeae66b4724d8926dd3d03ed682d\nauthor will <will@256k1.dev> 1790093124 +0100\ncommitter will <will@256k1.dev> 1790093757 +0100\n\nci: use POSIX threads for Nix Windows builds\n\nGuix release binaries use GCC's POSIX thread model, but the pinned\nNixpkgs compiler defaults to mcf.\n\nOverriding threadsCross on gcc14.cc does not recompute its\nalready-instantiated configure flags, and leaves wrapper dependency\nhandling tied to targetPackages.threads.\n\nTherefore here we instead replace the existing --enable-threads flag\ndirectly, and clear the target and wrapper extra-package dependencies.\n\n- `extraPackages = [ ]` stops the wrapper from adding `mcfgthread`\n  include/library paths or link dependencies.\n- `depsTargetTarget = [ ]` removes `mcfgthread` from GCC’s target-side\n  build dependencies.\n",
